    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.add_prefix_tree - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.add_prefix_tree.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.add_prefix_tree()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Add the prefix tree (trie) of a list of paths.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.add_prefix_tree()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Add the prefix tree (trie) of a list of paths.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.add_prefix_tree()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Add the prefix tree (trie) of a list of paths.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nAdd the prefix tree (trie) of a list of paths.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L20251-L20395){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.add_prefix_tree(\n    paths,\n    source_attr=\"source\",\n    type=None,\n    label=True,\n    rel=None,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Prefix tree](../assets/graphs/add-prefix-tree.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Three prefix trees (tries), each node labeled with the character it stands for and hung from an unlabeled root at the top. Paths that share a prefix share its nodes, so ab and ac branch below a single a, and every path ends at the one NIL node at the bottom, as in NetworkX.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nEach path is a sequence of items, such as the letters of a word. The prefix tree has a\nroot, one node for each distinct prefix of the paths, and a shared NIL node marking the\nend of a path: walking from the root, each step adds the next item, and paths that\nstart the same way share their first nodes. Each node stores the item it adds in the\n`source_attr=` node attribute; the NIL node stores `\"NIL\"` and the root nothing. A path\nthat ends at a node (because it is complete there) joins that node to NIL, so the\npaths can be read back as the root-to-NIL walks.\n\nNodes are created as in NetworkX's `prefix_tree()`: the root first, then NIL, then the\nprefixes depth first, each node's children in order of first appearance. NetworkX\nnumbers the root `0` and NIL `-1`; here they are simply the first two new nodes. Edges\nrun from each prefix to its extensions (and to NIL), which a directed graph keeps as\ntheir direction. The graph is appended without touching or connecting to existing\nnodes, and the whole construction is recorded as a single step.\n\nPrefix trees are useful for:\n\n- storing and searching a set of words or sequences by prefix (autocomplete, spell\n  checking, routing tables)\n- comparing sequences, such as event logs or clickstreams, by their shared beginnings\n- building directed trees from lists of root-to-leaf paths\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[paths]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [list]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The paths, each an iterable of hashable items (a string is a path of characters).\n\n<code>[source_attr]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[&quot;source&quot;]{.st}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Name of the node attribute that stores each node's item. Default is `\"source\"`, as\n    in NetworkX. Pass `None` to skip storing it.\n\n<code>[type]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Optional value stored in the `type` attribute of every new node. If `None` (default),\n    no `type` attribute is set.\n\n<code>[label]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[True]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True` (default), each new node is labelled with its node ID as a string; a label\n    that is already used raises `ValueError` before anything is added. If `False`, the\n    nodes are left unlabelled.\n\n<code>[rel]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Optional value stored in the `rel` attribute of every new edge. If `None` (default),\n    no `rel` attribute is set.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Self for method chaining. The graph is modified in place.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [TypeError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If a path is not iterable or holds an unhashable item.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~layout_bfs`) \n\n:   Draw the tree in layers from the root.\n\n[](`~add_balanced_tree`) \n\n:   Build a tree where every node has the same number of children.\n\n[](`~get_node_df`) \n\n:   Read the letter that each node adds.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nFour words share their first letters. The tree has a root, NIL, and one node per\ndistinct prefix:\n\n::: {#b20d6e4f .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\nwords = [\"ant\", \"and\", \"bee\", \"be\"]\ntree = ec.Graph(directed=True).add_prefix_tree(words)\n\ntree.count_nodes(), tree.count_edges()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n(9, 11)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nEach node keeps the letter it adds. `\"1\"` is the root and `\"2\"` the NIL node:\n\n::: {#d48cfb67 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ntree.get_node_df().select(\"label\", \"source\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```{=html}\n<div><style>\n.dataframe > thead > tr,\n.dataframe > tbody > tr {\n  text-align: right;\n  white-space: pre-wrap;\n}\n</style>\n<small>shape: (9, 2)</small><table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\"><thead><tr><th>label</th><th>source</th></tr><tr><td>str</td><td>str</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&quot;1&quot;</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;2&quot;</td><td>&quot;NIL&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;3&quot;</td><td>&quot;a&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;4&quot;</td><td>&quot;n&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;5&quot;</td><td>&quot;t&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;6&quot;</td><td>&quot;d&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;7&quot;</td><td>&quot;b&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;8&quot;</td><td>&quot;e&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;9&quot;</td><td>&quot;e&quot;</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nEvery word is a walk from the root to NIL, and \"be\" ends at the node that \"bee\" passes\nthrough:\n\n::: {#da3c93ce .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ntree.get_edges_str_repr()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```\n['1->3',\n '3->4',\n '4->5',\n '5->2',\n '4->6',\n '6->2',\n '1->7',\n '7->8',\n '8->2',\n '8->9',\n '9->2']\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Shared prefixes or none\n\nFour words each, drawn in layers from the root and labeled by letter. On the left\n\"cat\", \"car\", \"cab\" and \"cow\" share their first letter, and three of them the second,\nso `9` nodes hold them all. On the right \"cat\", \"dog\", \"emu\" and \"fox\" share nothing,\nand every letter needs its own node, `14` in all:\n\n::: {#27490f3e .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ndef prefix_tree(words):\n    tree = ec.Graph(directed=True).add_prefix_tree(words)\n    return tree.layout_bfs(source=1)\n\nshared = prefix_tree([\"cat\", \"car\", \"cab\", \"cow\"])\napart = prefix_tree([\"cat\", \"dog\", \"emu\", \"fox\"])\n\nshared.count_nodes(), apart.count_nodes()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```\n(9, 14)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {layout-ncol=\"2\"}\n\n::: {#024fa315 .cell execution_count=5}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nshared.plot(\n    layout=\"pos\", label_by=\"source\",\n    width=320, height=320, legend=False,\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=5}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1a